Requirements
Requirement	Module	Access program	Statement
view.1	view	view	The view MUST give, with no operand, the overview of every input the data bank holds, handing overview the data bank's _inputs and one relation days holding each input's days as zoom gives them.
view.2	view	view	The view MUST give, with an input's name as its one operand, that input's days, and with a day as its second operand, the turns of that day.
view.3	view	view	The view MUST give, with a position as its third operand, the details of that value, a position being that of a value stored on the day given.
view.5	view	view	The view MUST read the data bank only through its names, records and stored.
view.6	view	view	An input, day or position that does not exist MUST be refused with the reason no input, no day or no position, a space, and the operand.
view.9	view	view	More than three operands MUST be refused as too many operands.
view.8	view	view	The view MUST keep each level by filter's kept where --filter is given, lay it out by terminal's lay out, handing it whether standard output is a terminal as the view is handed it, and give it by terminal's page where standard output is a terminal and by terminal's write where it is not, and handing zoom the offset from UTC the view is handed.
overview.1	overview	overview	The overview MUST hold one record for each input of _inputs, in its order, its values as _inputs gives them, and its first, last and activity from that input's days.
overview.2	overview	overview	activity MUST hold one character for each day from first to last: for a day of n values, the block of the eight lower blocks from U+2581 to U+2588 whose rank is 8n divided by m, rounded up, m the most values of any day; and a space for a day with none.
zoom.3	zoom		A day MUST be the full date of a value's _time at the offset from UTC days and turns are handed.
zoom.1	zoom	days	days MUST hold, for each day an input has values and each event of that day, the number of values stored, the days in order.
zoom.2	zoom	turns	turns MUST hold one record for each value stored on the day, in the order stored.
zoom.4	zoom	turns	first line MUST be the text, up to its first line break, of the first instance of the value whose type is string and whose text is not empty, in the order the instances are written.
zoom.5	zoom	turns	agent, session, turn and model MUST each hold the text of the value's member that harness members names for that column, the first the value holds in that relation's order, and be empty where the value holds none.
filter.1	filter	kept	The option --filter MUST keep, at every level, the records for which the filter holds, as query decides.
details.1	details	details	details MUST give every record of the value in every sheet it gives, then its record of _stored, each sheet in its place in the order.
terminal.1	terminal	lay out	Where lay out is handed that standard output is not a terminal, a level MUST be written as MTSV text, by the generator.
terminal.2	terminal	lay out	Where lay out is handed that standard output is a terminal, each sheet MUST begin on a page of its own, FF before it, its sheet name on the first line, its header in bold, then its records, each field of the header and of the records padded to the width of its column's widest field, the fields of a line joined by the Value column gap.
terminal.3	terminal	lay out	A field's width MUST be the sum of its characters' widths, a wide or fullwidth character taking two columns and every other character one.
terminal.4	terminal	lay out	Bold MUST be set and reset by the select graphic rendition control function, with the parameters 1 and 0.
terminal.5	terminal	lay out	A control character in a field or sheet name MUST be written as its control picture, so that no field moves the cursor or changes the terminal.
terminal.6	terminal	write	The text MUST be written on standard output in UTF-8.
terminal.7	terminal	page	The text MUST be piped, in UTF-8, through the command the environment variable the Value pager variable names holds, run as the command string of sh -c, and through more where it is null or not set.
